            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46602",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled im ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled images, permitting a malicious or corrupt image containing a very large tile to cause unbounded memory consumption."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46602",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46602\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/image\nFixed Version: 0.43.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-46602](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46602)\nThe TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled images, permitting a malicious or corrupt image containing a very large tile to cause unbounded memory consumption.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46602**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/image|0.43.0|[CVE-2026-46602](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46602)|\n\nThe TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled images, permitting a malicious or corrupt image containing a very large tile to cause unbounded memory consumption."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46604",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder can panic when decoding an invalid image with an out- ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder can panic when decoding an invalid image with an out-of-bounds strip offset."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
